      "title": "Rust Docs Hosting",
      "author": "ZakAyesh",
      "number": 1985,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/docs",
      "body": "We have all of the rust docs merged together as a vocs documentation in the optimism monorepo. Current thoughts are we can host them:\n\n- Outside our main docs, and link to them. This may be easier for engineers to maintain since the docs live in the rust repo.\n\n- In docs.optimism.io. We would need to migrate the Vocs documentation to Mintlify. This provides a better developer experience as all our docs are in the same place.\n\nLet's discuss as a team, and then meet with the Rust team to decide.",
